<p>Cuba reported an island-wide power outage on Monday after the Energy and Mines Ministry and state utility UNE said the national electrical system had suffered a &quot;complete disconnection,&quot; or total collapse, leaving roughly 10 million to 11 million people without electricity across the island. Officials said they were still investigating the cause, but restoration work had already started, with power returning in some areas under emergency protocols. The blackout hit amid a broader energy crisis driven by fuel shortages, severe generation deficits, and mounting strain on aging infrastructure.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/t0hN70nqo8X4IOrPRGFg-6gto2Fo7R-6ypqfozjYIf0TcowOhIbWaBmjflpDU-sELcrbwNHrWBR89bv8417d8wA3ww6X4pdJibqw-bogOJl5gPLHDYjRz_DDIa-BTTfpfv5MIpHPbyf0id8YPhYXd5Pmo3VDbP-biucTALppxFieb6lp79BJVgR2C9q5q0Fd1fIt0OaqryrNI5VnnCCybpDOnhiKkESjwcKvjUzRH0s8f-0X46MLcjupuiU9JxCo9xgaYMeCRPRRH_yp_g' alt='People eat cups of soup outside during a blackout in Havana, March 4, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Recent cascade: ABC and CBS said Monday&#x27;s failure was the third major blackout in four months, coming just over a week after a massive outage affected western Cuba.</li><li>Import squeeze: The Straits Times said Cuba has received only two small oil vessels this year, underscoring the supply crunch behind prolonged generation deficits.</li><li>Public unrest: The Guardian said the latest outages helped spark a rare violent protest the previous weekend, showing how the electricity crisis is spilling into public order.</li><li>Critical services: RT reported that emergency protocols restored power in several areas, including Faustino Perez Hospital in Matanzas, pointing to priority support for essential services during the outage.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cuban government: The Energy and Mines Ministry and UNE said the outage was a complete disconnection of the national system and that restoration teams were at work while officials investigated the cause. (<a href='https://apnews.com/article/cuba-power-outage-electricity-4dcd92d4b7b3bbeda88622b543074ceb'>Associated Press</a>)</li><li>President Miguel Díaz-Canel: Díaz-Canel said Cuba had gone more than three months without oil shipments, highlighting the fuel-supply crisis surrounding the blackout. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/cuba-reports-island-wide-blackout-as-country-struggles-with-energy-crisis'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>US government: President Trump warned in January that he would impose tariffs on any country that sells or provides oil to Cuba, a step that multiple reports linked to the tighter supply environment. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/cuba-plunged-islandwide-blackout-power-crisis-worsens-photos-131139227'>ABC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/cuba-hit-by-island-wide-blackout-amid-trump-oil-blockade/a-76385816'>Cuba hit by island-wide blackout amid Trump oil blockade</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635264-cuba-blackout-us-blockade/'>Cuba suffers nationwide power outage amid US blockade</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/16/cuba-suffers-nationwide-blackout-after-total-collapse-of-national-power-grid'>Cuba suffers nationwide blackout after total collapse of national power grid</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/16/cuba-electrical-grid-collapses-amid-us-oil-blockade'>Cuba’s electrical grid collapses amid US oil blockade</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-16/cuba-is-left-without-power-due-to-the-complete-collapse-of-its-electrical-grid.html'>Cuba is left without power due to the complete collapse of its electrical grid</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/cuba-reports-island-wide-blackout-as-country-struggles-with-energy-crisis'>Cuba reports island-wide blackout as count